  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e46bef6c-34ce-590c-86c2-0e5945b7de8c" activityNameId="b23565c4-61bf-58cf-a294-352a179df203" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, SOEC, Stack</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electrolyzer production, 1MWe, SOEC, Stack
1 MWe Solid Oxide electrolyzer based on Niklas Gerloff, Comparative Life-Cycle-Assessment analysis of three major water electrolysis technologies while applying various energy scenarios for a greener hydrogen production, Journal of Energy Storage, Volume 43, 2021, https://doi.org/10.1/j.est0.20.1. Stack lifetime of 20'000 hours or 2.5 years @ 8'000 hours/year. Produced amount of H2 over 20 years: 3,776,000 kg. Amounts of lanthanum oxide and strontium carbonate are unsure.  Values have already account for 7 stack replacements over 20 years of use, excluding the initial component. For further secifications (e.g., efficiency, lifetime, etc.), refer to Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 83908945-c01e-33ee-aa47-4fd3a4ab9730
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_83908945-c01e-33ee-aa47-4fd3a4ab9730.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
